From: suds-mcduff <173517437+suds-mcduff@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] amdgpu: ps4 bridge connector: honour underscan properties

The PS4 MN864729 bridge connector attaches the legacy underscan,
underscan hborder and underscan vborder properties but its
drm_connector_funcs has no set_property hook, so userspace writes
(xrandr --set underscan on, KDE overscan) are accepted and never
applied. TVs that overscan HDMI therefore crop the desktop.

Forward just the three underscan properties to the common amdgpu
handler. It updates the encoder and re-runs the CRTC mode set, where
dce_v8_0_crtc_mode_set already calls the ATOM overscan and scaler
setup. Other properties remain ignored, as before.

Tested on a PS4 Slim (Baikal, Orbis 9.60) with v6.18.44-psx-ps4-baikal2 plus this
patch: xrandr underscan on with hborder 48 / vborder 27 shrinks the picture with
black borders and removes TV overscan cropping; each property change triggers one
mode set and the MN864729 link stays up.

Signed-off-by: suds-mcduff <173517437+suds-mcduff@users.noreply.github.com>
---
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_connectors.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_connectors.c
index bbbbca4..c9ab890 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_connectors.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_connectors.c
@@ -1600,11 +1600,33 @@ static const struct drm_connector_helper_funcs amdgpu_ps4_dp_connector_helper_fu
 	.best_encoder = amdgpu_connector_dvi_encoder,
 };
 
+/*
+ * The PS4 bridge connector exposes the legacy underscan properties but had no
+ * set_property hook, so writes were never applied. Forward only the three
+ * underscan properties to the common handler: it updates the encoder and
+ * re-runs the CRTC mode set, whose overscan and scaler setup then honour the
+ * borders. Other connector properties stay ignored as before.
+ */
+static int amdgpu_ps4_dp_connector_set_property(struct drm_connector *connector,
+						struct drm_property *property,
+						uint64_t val)
+{
+	struct amdgpu_device *adev = drm_to_adev(connector->dev);
+
+	if (property != adev->mode_info.underscan_property &&
+	    property != adev->mode_info.underscan_hborder_property &&
+	    property != adev->mode_info.underscan_vborder_property)
+		return 0;
+
+	pr_info("ps4_bridge: underscan property %s=%llu\n", property->name, val);
+	return amdgpu_connector_set_property(connector, property, val);
+}
+
 static const struct drm_connector_funcs amdgpu_ps4_dp_connector_funcs = {
 	.dpms = drm_helper_connector_dpms,
 	.detect = ps4_bridge_detect,
 	.fill_modes = drm_helper_probe_single_connector_modes,
-	//.set_property = amdgpu_connector_set_property,
+	.set_property = amdgpu_ps4_dp_connector_set_property,
 	.destroy = amdgpu_connector_destroy,
 	.force = amdgpu_connector_dvi_force,
 	.late_register = amdgpu_connector_late_register,
